    {
      "id": "rook-vell",
      "name": "Rook Vell",
      "species": "Human",
      "gender": "Male",
      "age": 32,
      "occupation": "Fence",
      "category": "criminal",
      "tags": [
        "fence",
        "alleys",
        "wanted"
      ],
      "description": "The fence people recommend when they actually want the job finished.",
      "biography": "Rook Vell's reputation as a fence was built one careful errand at a time around a respectable-looking back-room shop. Age 32 sits lightly on this Human, except when old debts creak. Watch long enough and you will see that he never sits with his back to a door. The ledger written in laundry marks is part tool, part talisman. Hunted by Serra; crew with Silk and Jax; rivals Kitty. He would trade sleep to buy legitimacy through a 'respectable' shopfront, yet stays wary of Serra getting a witness who won't scare. Current spark: Claimed ownership of the mill tunnel against Kitty Shade.",
      "personality": "Soft-spoken until principles are poked; never sits with his back to a door.",
      "motivation": "Turn today's scrapes into tomorrow's chance to buy legitimacy through a 'respectable' shopfront.",
      "secret": "Night thoughts keep returning to Serra getting a witness who won't scare, especially since: Claimed ownership of the mill tunnel against Kitty Shade.",
      "rumor": "Locals whisper that the ledger written in laundry marks once belonged to a traveler who vanished on the road.",
      "voice": "Quick local diction, then sudden silences that mean more than words.",
      "appearance": "Easy to spot near a respectable-looking back-room shop: human, practical layers, and the ledger written in laundry marks.",
