        "whistle"
      ],
      "description": "Gutter holds down rooftops above the alleys with callused competence and open ears.",
      "biography": "Some locals swear Gutter was born mid-shift at rooftops above the alleys; the truth is only slightly less devoted. This human lookout, now 25, treats competence like courtesy. He sleeps with a whistle between his teeth, never far from the chalk for marking safe tiles. Lookout for Rook; spotted by Tomas. Ask what he wants and he names it plainly: be paid enough to stop running messages. Ask what he dreads and the answer is Aya's arrows. Then comes the fresh problem—Signaled Tomas's patrol route to Rook's buyers.",
      "personality": "Warm with regulars, curt with wasters; sleeps with a whistle between his teeth.",
      "motivation": "Secure enough ground to be paid enough to stop running messages.",
      "secret": "Quietly arranging matters around this problem: Signaled Tomas's patrol route to Rook's buyers.",
      "rumor": "Customers claim Gutter knows which doors open after hours—if asked the right way.",
      "voice": "Polite public voice; sharper private asides when trust appears.",
