      ],
      "description": "Familiar face at river barges and warehouse doors; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Some locals swear Nedda was born mid-shift at river barges and warehouse doors; the truth is only slightly less devoted. This dwarf smuggler, now 90, treats competence like courtesy. She grins with the missing tooth facing customs, never far from the false-bottom grain sacks. Smuggler eyed by Brannic; paid by Orrin. Ask what she wants and she names it plainly: retire along the trade road with a clean name and dirty fortune. Ask what she dreads and the answer is Brannic measuring her draft again. Then comes the fresh problem—Moved lamp oil under grain manifests with Mael's unknowing help.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; grins with the missing tooth facing customs.",
      "motivation": "Protect her livelihood long enough to retire along the trade road with a clean name and dirty fortune.",
