      "description": "Familiar face at doorways after dark; useful, stubborn, and hard to surprise.",
      "biography": "Some locals swear Bask was born mid-shift at doorways after dark; the truth is only slightly less devoted. This half-orc debt collector, now 35, treats competence like courtesy. He knocks politely, then harder, never far from the leather gloves lined with coin weights. Marrow's collector; clashed with Dorn. Ask what he wants and he names it plainly: earn Marrow's partnership, not just wages. Ask what he dreads and the answer is Dorn catching him in public again. Then comes the fresh problem—Warned a baker that 'accidents' happen to ovens behind on interest.",
      "personality": "Proud of competence more than praise; knocks politely, then harder.",
      "motivation": "Protect his livelihood long enough to earn Marrow's partnership, not just wages.",
