      ],
      "description": "A sewer runner rooted at storm drains and undercroft tunnels, known for how he apologizes to rats before he traps them.",
      "biography": "Mouse Pip's reputation as a sewer runner was built one careful errand at a time around storm drains and undercroft tunnels. Age 21 sits lightly on this Halfling, except when old debts creak. Watch long enough and you will see that he apologizes to rats before he traps them. The oilskin map folio of tunnels is part tool, part talisman. Knows sewers; fed by Pola; tracked by Kessa. He would trade sleep to sell his maps to someone who won't kill him after, yet stays wary of being sealed in below during a storm. Current spark: His tunnel sketch matches Wren's joke map and Rina's overheard 'mill tunnel'.",
      "personality": "Steady and sharp-eyed; apologizes to rats before he traps them.",
      "motivation": "To sell his maps to someone who won't kill him after, even while fearing being sealed in below during a storm.",
      "secret": "Knows more about this than he admits: His tunnel sketch matches Wren's joke map and Rina's overheard 'mill tunnel'.",
      "rumor": "A smugglers' mark was seen near storm drains and undercroft tunnels on a night Mouse worked late.",
      "voice": "Low and practical, with a habit of repeating the important clause once.",
